infographic sequence-ascending-steps
data
  title The three-tier payload length encoding
  desc The 7-bit length field escalates: pay more header bytes only when the payload outgrows the previous tier
  order asc
  sequences
    - label Length 0-125 — inline 7-bit field
      desc The length byte holds the real length. No extension. Header stays at 2 bytes — the minimum WebSocket frame.
    - label Length 126 — uint16 extension
      desc The 7-bit field signals 126; the next 2 bytes carry the real length, up to 65,535 bytes. Header grows by +2 bytes.
    - label Length 127 — uint64 extension
      desc The 7-bit field signals 127; the next 8 bytes carry the real length. Header grows by +8 bytes, addressing payloads far beyond any practical message.
theme
  palette #14b8a6 #f59e0b #f43f5e
